# Gate G-M8 baseline (scripts/gates/mls-vendored-clock-log.sh = dm-vendored-clock-log.sh --graph mls;
# Phase 10 design faza10-forum.md §3.6, §13.1 G-M8; T3, T33; slice S2a). The compiled library code of
# every crate of `cargo tree -p ghost-client-mls -e normal --features jni-bridge` on
# aarch64-linux-android and x86_64-linux-android, with the features each package has in the shipped
# library (`cargo tree -p ghost-client-net`; slice S2b links the crate there with its JNI export),
# merged over both triples. Kinds: [lib] linked into the library; [proc-macro] and
# [build-time] run only while compiling. Every site, directive and note line ends in its reason after
# two spaces and '#'. An entry the scan finds and this file lacks fails the gate (unjustified); an
# entry here the scan no longer finds fails it too (stale). Regenerate at a pin change with
# GHOST_G_R8_PRINT=1 and complete every '# UNJUSTIFIED' by review, never by copy.
#
# Seeded 2026-09-29 by slice S2a. Entries identical to the DM graph's (dm-vendored-clock-log.baseline:
# serde_core, libc, rand, memchr, the proc-macro and build-time crates, ...) carry the reasons reviewed
# there. New with the OpenMLS stack: OpenMLS's clock sites of design §3.6 (past_secrets.rs:80,105
# stamps rewritten to the call's day; 234,254 never called; 271 called with UNIX_EPOCH only;
# lifetime.rs:66 never called, 88/93 never refusing the constant lifetime), its log facade calls (no
# logger installed, G-M4), the memory storage GHOST never uses, rayon's worker parking and abort
# guard, the build directives of crossbeam, zerocopy, rayon-core and libcrux-aes (G-M9), and the
# crate's own UNIX_EPOCH constant. The review of S2a (F5, §19.31) added the patterns UNIX_EPOCH and
# elapsed (a clock read through the imported constant or a clock value's method): 11 more sites, each
# justified below — the crate's import and its one use in sweep_past, OpenMLS's time-based deletion
# and lifetime code, a rayon-core test module and serde's re-export.
#
# Slice S2b (design §19.32) scans the graph as the shipped library links it: `jni-bridge` on, each
# package with its features in ghost-client-net's graph. Measured: of S2a's entries only the crate's
# own sweep_past line moved (1847 -> 1947: the invite and join functions S2b adds above it), and the
# feature unification adds no site; new are the `jni` subtree's 9 crates, 15 build directives
# (jni-sys 0.3.1, thiserror 1.0.69) and jni's 23 log facade sites — each identical to the DM graph's
# entry and carrying the reason reviewed there (G-R4, G-R8).

# Sites (clock, logging, printing, network):
